{"strongs": "H2459", "word": "חֵ֫לֶב", "translit": "che.lev", "root": "חלב", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "fat", "definition": "I. חֵ֫לֶב noun masculine Exod 29:13 fat (Late Hebrew id., fat , so Phoenician חלב (probably); Aramaic (also diaphragm in Lexicons, see PS 1274 ) originally diaphragm, midriff ; Arabic , including midriff-fat , RS Semitic i. 360 ); — ׳ ח absolute Lev 3:16 + 40 t.; construct Gen 45:18 + 21 t.; suffix חֶלְבּוֺ Lev 3:9 + 6 t.; חֶלְבָּהּ Lev 4:31 ; Lev 4:35 , חֶלְבָּם Num 18:17 , חֶלְבָּ֫מוֺ Ps 17:10 , חֶלְבְּהֶ֫ן Lev 8:16 ; Lev 8:25 (read plural noun חלביהן Samaritan Di ); plural הַחֲלָבִים Lev 8:26 + 7 t.; construct חֶלְבֵי Lev 6:5 + 4 t.; suffix חֶלְבֵהֶן Gen 4:4 ( חלביהן Samaritan Di , compare Lev 8:16 ; Lev 8:25 above); — 1. fat of human body Judg 3:22 (covering intestines); גִּבּוֺרִים ׳ ח 2Sam 1:22 as smearing warrior's shield; of grossness of wicked כִּסָּה פָּנָיו בְּחֶלְבּוֺ Job 15:27 fat (of midriff) figurative of unreceptive heart סָֽגְרוּ ׳ ח Ps 17:10 , see also Ps 73:7 (read מֵחֵלֶב עֲוֺנָמוֺ for מחלב עֵינֵמוֺ ᵐ5 ᵑ6 Hi Ew Ol De Che Bae and others); ׳ טָפַשׁ כַּח לִבָּם Ps 119:70 i.e. their heart is as unresponsive as the midriff-fat near it. 2. fat of beasts: \\ \\ a. as rich food (poetry) Deut 32:14 and in simile Ps 63:6 (|| דֶּשֶׁן ); so ᵑ0 Ezek 34:3 (but read הֶחָלָב , see חָלָב ), Ezek 39:19 ( ᵑ6 Co בשׂר ). \\ \\ b. especially as offered in sacrifice, singular, to ׳ י Exod 23:18 ( J E ), 1Sam 2:15 ; 1Sam 2:16 ; Exod 29:13 (twice in verse); Exod 29:22 (3 t. in verse); Lev 3:3 (twice in verse); Lev 3:4 ; Lev 3:9 (3 t. in verse); Lev 3:10 ; Lev 3:14 (twice in verse); Lev 3:15 + 23 t. Leviticus; Num 18:17 (all P ), Lev 17:6 ( H ), 1Sam 15:22 ; Isa 1:11 ; Isa 43:24 ; Ezek 44:7 ; Ezek 44:15 see Isa 34:6 (twice in verse); Isa 34:7 of fat of Edomites slaughtered by ׳ י 's sword (under figure of lambs, rams, and bulls); as eaten by (strange) gods Deut 32:38 (poetry), not to be eaten by men Lev 3:17 ; Lev 7:23 ; Lev 7:24 (twice in verse); Lev 7:25 (all P ); also plural, fat parts or pieces Gen 4:4 ( J ) Lev 6:5 + 8 t. Leviticus; 1Kgs 8:64 (twice in verse); 2Chr 7:7 (twice in verse); 2Chr 29:35 ; 2Chr 35:14 . 3. choicest, best part of products of land Gen 45:18 ( E ), specifically of oil Num 18:12 and wine v Num 18:12 of corn and oil v Num 18:29 v Num 18:30 v Num 18:32 also (poetry) כִּלְיוֺת חִטָּה ׳ ח Deut 32:14 kidney-fat of wheat (i.e. the very choicest, compare Isa 34:6 ), חִטָּה ׳ ח Ps 81:17 , חִטִּים ׳ ח Ps 147:14 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2747')\">BDB2747</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H2459')\">H2459</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2746')\">BDB2746</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2748')\">BDB2748</entry></div><p> I. <bdbheb>חֵ֫לֶב</bdbheb> <b>noun masculine</b><sup><ref ref=\"Exod 29:13\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"29\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"29\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(2,29,13)\">Exod 29:13</ref></sup> <highlightword>fat</highlightword> (Late Hebrew <highlight>id., fat</highlight>, so Phoenician <bdbheb>חלב</bdbheb> (probably); Aramaic <placeholder1749/> (also <highlight>diaphragm</highlight> in Lexicons, see <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('PS')\">PS<sup>1274</sup></lookup>) originally <highlight>diaphragm, midriff</highlight>; Arabic <placeholder1750/>, including <highlight>midriff-fat</highlight>, <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('RS')\">RS<sup>Semitic i. 360</sup></lookup>); — <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>ח</bdbheb> absolute <ref ref=\"Lev 3:16\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(3,3,16)\">Lev 3:16</ref> + 40 t.; construct <ref ref=\"Gen 45:18\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"45\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"45\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(1,45,18)\">Gen 45:18</ref> + 21 t.; suffix <bdbheb>חֶלְבּוֺ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Lev 3:9\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(3,3,9)\">Lev 3:9</ref> + 6 t.; <bdbheb>חֶלְבָּהּ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Lev 4:31\" b=\"3\" cBegin=